course: dictionary
lesson: 4374
title: A word with a history
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are old names for people, and they can hurt even when they were once used without thinking. «Gypsy and Traveller people are just people, each different.» This sentence reminds us that people are individuals, not one picture in our heads.
explain: Gypsy is an old name for a person of the Romani people (Roma). Their ancestors came from India long ago and travelled through Europe. Many Romani people still travel, and many live in houses.
explain: Some people find «gypsy» hurtful, so many now say «Romani» or «Roma». When you are not sure, use the name people use for themselves.
fact: Gypsy is an old name for the Romani people (Roma).
fact: The Romani people came from India long ago and have their own language and culture.
fact: Many Romani people have been treated unfairly over history, and many were killed in the Holocaust.
fact: Some people find «gypsy» hurtful, so «Romani» or «Roma» is the safer choice.
fact: As an adjective, gypsy describes something of a travelling kind, such as a gypsy caravan.
exercise: «Gypsy and Traveller people are just people, each different.» What is the main idea of this sentence? | *People from these communities are all different, like everyone else | Gypsies only ever live outside | All gypsies are exactly the same | Travellers should only live in caravans
exercise: Which names do many people choose to use for the Romani people? | *Romani or Roma | Travellers only | Caravan people | Gipsy only
exercise: In «a gypsy caravan», what kind of word is gypsy? | A verb, meaning to travel | A name for a river | *An adjective, describing the caravan | A number
test: Why do many people prefer the word Romani to gypsy? | *Because some find gypsy hurtful | Because gypsy means a colour | Because it is shorter | Because it is a new word
test: Where did the Romani people's ancestors come from long ago? | *India | Egypt | Australia | Scotland
exam: Which word is the safest to use for the Romani people when you are not sure what they prefer? | Gypsy | Traveller only | Caravan people | *Romani or Roma
